 R←Test_Server_125(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;c;q;r;noOf
⍝ Provoke an error in the application's `OnHeader` handler.
⍝ The client must get a 500, HandleError must save a crash report, and the server must carry on:
⍝ up to RumbaLean 3.5.2 such an error stopped the server with ⎕OFF 125.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If ##.FilesAndDirs.IsDir ∆GetCrashFolder
     noOf←≢##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder,'/*.html'
 :Else
     noOf←0
 :EndIf

 c←∆NewClient
 q←Rumba.NewRequest 0
 q.RequestTarget←'/crash-in-header'
 r←c Rumba.SendAndReceive q

 →T.PassesIf r.StatusCode=500
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<h1>500: Internal Server Error</h1>'⍷r.Content
 →T.PassesIf(noOf+1)=≢##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder,'/*.html'

 c←∆NewClient                                       ⍝ The server closed the connection after the 500
 q←Rumba.NewRequest 0
 q.RequestTarget←'/groups'                          ⍝ Not '/packages': Test_Server_999 counts those
 r←c Rumba.SendAndReceive q
 →T.PassesIf r.StatusCode=200                       ⍝ The server is still running

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
